				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				501,
				12
			],
			"Message": "feat(Cocoon/Integration): Enhance Mountain client integration with comprehensive configuration and TypeScript tooling\n\nThis commit significantly improves Cocoon's Mountain client integration by introducing a comprehensive configuration management system (`MountainConfig`), enhancing generated gRPC types (`Vine_pb.d.ts`), and creating a high-level client wrapper (`MountainClient`) that simplifies interaction with Mountain's gRPC services.\n\nThe new `MountainConfig` interface provides granular control over gRPC connection settings including timeout values, retry policies, TLS configuration, and auto-reconnect behavior, with built-in validation and environment variable support. This aligns with Land's declarative effects architecture by providing structured configuration management for the critical Mountain-to-Cocoon communication layer.\n\nAdditionally, the APIFactoryService has been enhanced with Microsoft VSCode API patterns, adding comprehensive input validation, security patterns, and support for additional APIs (notebooks, tests, comments, telemetry). This improves compatibility with VS Code extensions while maintaining the Land ecosystem's security principles.\n\nTypeScript dependencies and configuration have been updated to support the enhanced tooling, including better protocol buffer integration and improved path mapping for VSCode dependencies.",
			"SHA": "daa24fc6f3d9a7f9a6e07f21651a8cb359298e1d"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-01-30T11:05:30Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				497,
				3
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Cocoon/GRPCServerService): Refactor gRPC server methods to use async/await\n\nThis commit refactors the GRPCServerService in Cocoon to transition from callback-based gRPC methods to promise-based async/await patterns. This change aligns with Land's Effect-TS architecture, promoting more declarative and composable asynchronous code.\n\nThe key modifications include updating import statements to use specific gRPC components, modifying service methods to return promises, and improving error handling by including error objects in responses. The ServiceMapping.ts file is also updated to include ModuleInterceptorService imports, enhancing interception capabilities.\n\nThis refactor improves code readability, aligns with modern TypeScript practices, and better integrates with Cocoon's effects-based service layer, facilitating easier testing and maintenance.",
			"SHA": "05b34bae9cd6317a5300bea6123e81c97e26eadc"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-01-30T10:55:29Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				497,
				2
			],
			"Message": "test(Cocoon/Synchronization): Add comprehensive test suite for SynchronizationService\n\nThis commit introduces extensive unit tests for the SynchronizationService, reinforcing the reliability enhancements in Cocoon's document synchronization capabilities with the Mountain backend. The test suite validates critical functionality including connection management, real-time document synchronization, conflict resolution, error handling with circuit breaker logic, performance monitoring, and resource cleanup.\n\nThe tests are built using Vitest and mock Tauri IPC commands to simulate interactions with Mountain's gRPC interface, ensuring robust validation of synchronization logic. This enhances Cocoon's operational resilience by catching regressions early and providing confidence in the synchronization layer's behavior under various conditions, crucial for maintaining consistent state between the extension host and Mountain in the Land ecosystem.",
			"SHA": "e432451763dbc7e88778b77f64634ba8652b8596"
		}
	],
